Order matters. I'll write a scanner:

```dart
final _inline = RegExp(
  r'!\[([^\]]*)\]\(([^)\s]+)(?:\s+"([^"]*)")?\)'   // image
  r'|\[([^\]]+)\]\(([^)\s]+)(?:\s+"([^"]*)")?\)'    // link
  r'|`([^`]+)`'                                      // code
  r'|\*\*([^*]+)\*\*'                                // bold
  r'|(?<!\*)\*([^*\n]+)\*(?!\*)'                     // em — dart regex supports lookbehind? Dart RegExp is JS-like: NO lookbehind!
```

Dart RegExp: no lookbehind support (lookAHEAD is supported). So em matching without lookbehind: `\*([^*\n]+)\*` and ensure bold processed first (regex alternation order: bold tried at each position before em, so `**x**` matches bold at position). But overlapping: for `**bold**`, at pos of first `*`, alternation tries bold first → matches `**bold**`. Good. For `a *b* c`: at `*` (single), bold fails, em matches `*b*`. Edge `*a **b** c*` — rare; acceptable.

